  "secEn": [
    {
      "h": "Adults \u2014 minimum times",
      "items": [
        "Clear fluids: 2 h (ASA) \u2014 a more liberal approach is encouraged",
        "Light meal: ~6 h or longer",
        "Fat/protein-rich meal: ~8 h or longer",
        "The \"or longer\" stresses that individual assessment outweighs generic advice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Children (ESAIC 2022)",
      "items": [
        "Clear fluids: 1 h \u2014 a major change in paediatric practice",
        "Breast milk: 3 h \u00B7 Infant formula: 4 h",
        "Solids/milk: 6 h \u00B7 Rich meal: 8 h",
        "Avoid prolonged fasting: it may be associated with lower SBP during anaesthesia (>8 h: \u2193SBP/MAP after induction) and ketone body accumulation (ESAIC 2022, Suggestions 3\u20134)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Do not cancel automatically",
      "items": [
        "Clear fluid intake <2 h preop alone does NOT justify postponing or cancelling",
        "Hospitals are encouraged to develop protocols that shorten liquid fasting times",
        "Prolonged fasting: dehydration, insulin resistance, increased stress response, delirium (ESAIC)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Higher risk \u2014 individualise",
      "items": [
        "GLP-1 agonists: delayed gastric emptying (see Periop meds \u2192 Diabetes)",
        "Diabetic gastroparesis \u00B7 emergency \u00B7 pregnancy \u00B7 ileus \u00B7 severe GORD",
        "Gastric ultrasound: assess contents when history is uncertain (see Tools \u2192 Gastric ultrasound)",
        "US findings guide timing, anaesthetic technique and airway management"
      ]
    }
  ],
