  "secEn": [
    {
      "h": "The rule",
      "items": [
        "Quantitative monitoring \u2014 not clinical assessment, not a simple nerve stimulator \u00B7 in children EMG rather than AMG (ESAIC/ESPA 2025)",
        "Site: adductor pollicis, ulnar nerve stimulation",
        "BEFORE extubation confirm TOFr \u2265 0.9",
        "Clinical/qualitative assessment leaves residual block undetected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Depth of block",
      "items": [
        "Deep: TOF count 0 \u00B7 PTC \u22651",
        "Moderate: TOF count 1\u20133",
        "Shallow: TOFr < 0.4",
        "Minimal: TOFr 0.4 \u2013 <0.9",
        "Adequate recovery: TOFr \u2265 0.9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Reversal \u2014 adults",
      "items": [
        "Sugammadex: from deep, moderate or shallow block (rocuronium/vecuronium)",
        "Neostigmine: reasonable alternative only from minimal block (TOFr 0.4 \u2013 <0.9)",
        "ESAIC: do not give neostigmine before TOFr > 0.2 \u2014 a common error",
        "Sugammadex doses: see Meds \u2192 Sugammadex (2 / 4 / 16 mg/kg)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Children (ESAIC/ESPA 2025)",
      "items": [
        "Same rule: quantitative monitoring and TOFr \u2265 0.9 before extubation",
        "If an NMBA is needed \u2192 rocuronium or vecuronium (reversible with sugammadex)",
        "Sugammadex OVER neostigmine \u2014 faster, more predictable and safer recovery",
        "Age < 2 years: sugammadex safe at the same dose range as children/adults",
        "Titrate NMBA dose to quantitative monitoring",
        "Avoid excessive rocuronium doses \u2014 risk of residual block/recurarisation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Special situations",
      "items": [
        "Muscular dystrophy: quantitative monitoring is particularly important (delayed onset, prolonged recovery) \u00B7 no neostigmine in myasthenic disorders",
        "No succinylcholine in Duchenne/Becker \u2014 rhabdomyolysis, hyperkalaemia, arrest \u00B7 for RSI rocuronium rather than succinylcholine",
        "< 2 years or large total rocuronium/vecuronium dose: extended PACU observation",
        "Neonates/infants: an NMBA is recommended to facilitate tracheal intubation in the OR"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "srcEl": "ASA Practice Guidelines for Monitoring and Antagonism of Neuromuscular Blockade (2023) \u00B7 ESAIC, Eur J Anaesthesiol 2023 \u00B7 2025 ESAIC and ESPA Guidelines on neuromuscular block in anaesthetised children: indications, monitoring and reversal, Eur J Anaesthesiol.",
